<item><title><![CDATA[IR Y VENIR: dos verbos que traen de cabeza a muchos]]></title><description><![CDATA[If you mix up ir and venir, this post is for you!]]></description><link>https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/ir-y-venir-dos-verbos-que-traen-de</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/ir-y-venir-dos-verbos-que-traen-de</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Learning Spanish with Myriam]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 06:27:12 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong><span>This post is written in Spanish on purpose. You don&#8217;t need to understand every word, just keep reading.</span></strong></p><p><strong>Ir</strong> y <strong>venir</strong> son dos verbos que parecen estar emparejados para hacernos la vida un poquito m&#225;s dif&#237;cil. &#128517;</p><p>Y es que no solo pueden resultar confusos por su significado, sino tambi&#233;n por sus conjugaciones.</p><p>Sinceramente, yo no entiendo muy bien <strong>qui&#233;n dise&#241;&#243; las conjugaciones del verbo IR</strong>. &#161;No tienen ning&#250;n sentido! &#128514;</p><p><strong>Honestly,I feel your pain.</strong></p><p>Mira este peque&#241;o ejemplo con la primera persona del singular:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Yo voy</strong> &#8594; presente de indicativo</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo fui</strong> &#8594; pret&#233;rito indefinido</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo iba</strong> &#8594; pret&#233;rito imperfecto</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo he ido</strong> &#8594; pret&#233;rito perfecto compuesto</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo vaya</strong> &#8594; presente de subjuntivo</p></li></ul><p><strong>WTF?!</strong> &#129327; &#161;Y del gerundio mejor ni hablamos!</p><p>En fin&#8230; sigamos.</p><p>Por otro lado, tenemos <strong>venir</strong>:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Yo vengo</strong> &#8594; presente de indicativo</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo vine</strong> &#8594; pret&#233;rito indefinido</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo ven&#237;a</strong> &#8594; pret&#233;rito imperfecto</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo he venido</strong> &#8594; pret&#233;rito perfecto compuesto</p></li><li><p><strong>Yo venga</strong> &#8594; presente de subjuntivo</p></li></ul><p>Comparado con <strong>ir</strong>, tiene un poquito m&#225;s de sentido&#8230; pero tampoco es para tirar cohetes. &#128514;</p><p>Bueno, a lo que <strong>ven&#237;amos</strong>. &#128064;</p><p>En realidad, hoy me quer&#237;a centrar m&#225;s en el <strong>significado</strong>.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg" width="1200" height="1600" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1600,&quot;width&quot;:1200,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:321225,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/i/215628805?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HHJx!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f314b7a-fa0b-4164-9c56-8c5d20f7493a_1200x1600.jpeg 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h2>Entonces&#8230; &#191;Cu&#225;ndo usamos IR y cu&#225;ndo usamos VENIR?</h2><p>La clave est&#225; en <strong>el punto de referencia</strong>.</p><p>&#128073; Usamos <strong>IR</strong> cuando hablamos de un desplazamiento <strong>desde el lugar en el que estamos hacia otro lugar</strong>.</p><p>&#128073; Usamos <strong>VENIR</strong> cuando hablamos de un desplazamiento <strong>hacia el lugar en el que estamos o hacia el lugar de referencia</strong>.</p><p>Para. Vuelve a leer lo anterior &#128070;&#127996;</p><p>Por ejemplo:</p><p><strong>Yo voy todos los meses al cine.</strong></p><p>Si estoy en casa cuando digo esto, el movimiento es:</p><p><strong>CASA &#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&gt; CINE</strong></p><p>Voy <strong>desde donde estoy</strong> hasta el cine.</p><p>Pero imagina ahora que estoy hablando con alguien <strong>en el cine</strong>:</p><p><strong>Yo vengo todos los meses al cine.</strong></p><p>El movimiento es:</p><p><strong>CINE &lt;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472; CASA</strong></p><p>Pero esta vez, el punto de referencia es <strong>el cine</strong>, donde est&#225; la persona con la que estoy hablando.</p><p>Y lo mismo ocurre con <strong>Barcelona</strong>:</p><p><strong>He venido a Barcelona muchas veces.</strong></p><p>&#128073; Estoy <strong>en Barcelona</strong> cuando digo esta frase.</p><p>En cambio:</p><p><strong>He ido a Barcelona muchas veces.</strong></p><p>&#128073; No estoy en Barcelona cuando digo esto. Podr&#237;a estar en <strong>Salou, Madrid, Par&#237;s, Granada, Minnesota u Ottawa</strong>. &#128514;</p><p>La idea clave es:</p><p><strong>IR &#8594; hacia otro lugar</strong><br><strong>VENIR &#8594; hacia aqu&#237; / hacia el lugar en el que estoy</strong></p><p>Y s&#237;, s&#233; lo que est&#225;s pensando&#8230;</p><p><strong>&#191;Por qu&#233; tiene que ser tan complicado?</strong> &#128514;</p><h3>&#129504; &#191;IR o VENIR?</h3><p>Lee cada situaci&#243;n y completa con la forma correcta de <strong>ir</strong> o <strong>venir</strong>.</p><p><strong>Si quieres ver los ejercicios relacionados con el post, &#161;suscr&#237;bete, es gratis!</strong></p><p>Enjoying these articles? Subscribe and receive new posts directly in your inbox so you never miss one. Subscriptions are free, and if you&#8217;d like to support my work, you can also become a paid subscriber.</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p>Los ejercicios incluyen diferentes <strong>tiempos verbales y personas</strong>, y tendr&#225;s que fijarte bien en el <strong>contexto</strong> para elegir el verbo correcto.</p><p>Porque con <em>ir</em> y <em>venir</em>&#8230; &#161;el contexto lo es todo! &#128517;</p><p>&#191;Qu&#233; tal te ha ido con los ejercicios? </p><p>Espero que despu&#233;s de esta explicaci&#243;n ya tengas un poquito m&#225;s claro la diferencia entre IR y VENIR. </p><p>Cu&#233;ntame si hay alguna otra pareja de verbos que se te est&#225; atragantando en espa&#241;ol. </p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/ir-y-venir-dos-verbos-que-traen-de/comments&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Leave a comment&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/ir-y-venir-dos-verbos-que-traen-de/comments"><span>Leave a comment</span></a></p><p>And as always, <span>If you enjoyed this article, I&#8217;d be incredibly grateful if you tapped the &#10084;&#65039; below and shared it with someone who might find it useful.</span></p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/ir-y-venir-dos-verbos-que-traen-de?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/ir-y-venir-dos-verbos-que-traen-de?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share"><span>Share</span></a></p><p><span>&#161;Nos vemos a la semana que viene!</span></p><p><span>Myriam</span></p><p><span>P.S. If you&#8217;re interested in 1:1 Spanish lessons, you can find </span><a href="https://dailypush.es/"><span>all the information here.</span></a></p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded></item>